---
# Rendered by enso-agent-bootstrap (lib/workflow.sh) from the agent's conf. Re-running
# install refreshes this file and keeps `enabled`; change it through the conf.
name: ${WORKFLOW_NAME}
workflow: 2
enabled: ${ENABLED}
repo: ${REPO_DIR}
base: ${WORKFLOW_BASE}
setup: ${SETUP}
max_concurrency: ${WORKFLOW_MAX_CONCURRENCY}
paths:
  full: [pm, build, review, publish, qa, signoff, merge]
  short: [pm, build, review, publish, merge]
default_path: full
stages:
- name: pm
  worktree: false
  routes: [full, short]
  default_route: full
  output: >-
    Brief: goal, acceptance criteria, out of scope, surfaces touched, decisions with who
    made them and when, notes for Build, and the route.
  instructions: >-
    Turn the request into a brief Build can work from without guessing. Ask the client one
    standalone question when a customer decision is missing; never invent one. A
    well-specified ticket passes straight through.
- name: build
  inputs: [request, pm]
  worktree: true
  max_repairs: 2
  output: The candidate commits, what changed, tests added, docs touched.
  instructions: Implement the brief in the task worktree. Commit everything; never push.
  checks:
${BUILD_CHECKS}
- name: review
  inputs: [request, pm, build]
  worktree: true
  return_to: build
  max_returns: 2
  output: Accept with a summary for the person who will try it, or specific findings.
  instructions: A second agent reviews the exact candidate against the brief.
- name: publish
  inputs: [request, pm, build, review]
  worktree: true
  command: ./publish-pr.sh
  output: The pull request for the reviewed candidate.
- name: qa
  inputs: [pm, build, review, publish]
  worktree: true
  return_to: build
  max_returns: 1
  output: >-
    What was exercised on the preview and the result; Before and After screenshots of the
    same view for visible changes.
  instructions: Exercise the user journey the brief describes on the PR's preview deployment.
- name: signoff
  inputs: [pm, review, publish, qa]
  human: true
  return_to: build
  output: The approver's explicit approval of this version.
- name: merge
  inputs: [build, review, publish, "qa?", "signoff?"]
  worktree: true
  command: ./merge-pr.sh
  return_to: build
  max_returns: 2
  output: The merge commit on ${WORKFLOW_BASE}.
hooks:
  after_transition: ./lore-bridge.sh transition
  after:blocked: ./notify.sh
  after:signoff: ./notify.sh
---

${WORKFLOW_NAME} development workflow. Tasks come from Lore tickets assigned to
${LORE_ASSIGNEE} (the `${JOB_PREFIX}-lore-dispatch` job). Questions, signoff requests and
failures are posted by `notify.sh`; the PR is opened by `publish-pr.sh` and merged by
`merge-pr.sh` once CI passes on the approved head.
